- Story & Context: In the refectory of Aethelgard, Brother Silas watched the clock shatter against the wall during a fever dream, realizing the gears were actually tiny trapped moths hitting the glass. "The rhythm isn't for you, it’s for the wreckage" he muttered while wiring his patch cables to mimic the sound of insect wings beating against a cathedral window.
